Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/BrucePerens/hams_open/tree/main/hardware/lenovo_thinkpad_yoga_11e

Package: lenovo-thinkpad-yoga-11e-support
Architecture: all
Depends: convertible-power (>= 1.0.3), convertible-helper (>= 1.4.0), iio-sensor-proxy, udev, network-manager, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: thermald, smartmontools, firmware-iwlwifi
Description: Lenovo ThinkPad Yoga 11e demo-laptop support for Debian
 Settings for the first-generation Lenovo ThinkPad Yoga 11e convertible on a
 stock Debian GNOME desktop: it pulls in convertible-power (maximum
 performance on AC, maximum battery life on battery, no inactivity suspend at
 the login screen on AC) and convertible-helper (screen upright when leaving
 tablet mode, on-screen keyboard at the login screen), and adds this laptop's
 settings: lid ignored and no inactivity suspend on AC, screen off after 5
 minutes, Wi-Fi power saving off.
 .
 The settings are applied only when the DMI product version is "ThinkPad Yoga 11e".
